## 📖 Overview

**Passive Image Forgery Detection** is a full-stack forensic tool that detects whether an image has been digitally tampered with — specifically **copy-move** and **splicing** forgeries — *without* relying on any embedded watermark or metadata (hence "passive").

It fuses three techniques into one hybrid detection pipeline:

- 🧠 **DCNN** *(Deep CNN)* — learns high-level tamper artifacts & texture inconsistencies
- 🧩 **SLIC** *(Superpixel Segmentation)* — breaks the image into perceptually meaningful regions for localization
- 🔑 **SIFT** *(Keypoint Matching)* — detects duplicated regions characteristic of copy-move attacks

Trained and benchmarked on the **CASIA v1.0** dataset, and served through a live web app where anyone can upload an image and get an instant forgery verdict.

<br/>

## ✨ Features

- 🖼️ Drag-and-drop image upload — get a prediction in seconds
- 🎯 Region localization — highlights *where* tampering likely occurred, not just *if*
- 🔀 Dual forgery detection — handles both copy-move and splicing
- ⚡ Fast inference through a lightweight backend API
- 🌐 Deployed & live at [forensic-vision.vercel.app](https://forensic-vision.vercel.app)
- 📊 Trained & validated on CASIA v1.0 with reproducible training scripts

<br/>

## ⚙️ How It Works

<details open>
<summary><b>Click to expand / collapse the pipeline diagram</b></summary>

<br/>

```
                     ┌────────────────────┐
                     │   Uploaded Image    │
                     └─────────┬───────────┘
                               │
              ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
              ▼                ▼                 ▼
      ┌───────────────┐ ┌─────────────┐  ┌───────────────┐
      │  DCNN Branch   │ │ SLIC Branch │  │  SIFT Branch  │
      │ (tamper feats) │ │ (superpixel │  │  (keypoint    │
      │                │ │ segmentation)│  │   matching)   │
      └───────┬────────┘ └──────┬──────┘  └───────┬───────┘
              │                 │                  │
              └─────────────────┼──────────────────┘
                                 ▼
                    ┌────────────────────────┐
                    │   Fusion / Classifier    │
                    └────────────┬─────────────┘
                                 ▼
                    ┌────────────────────────┐
                    │  Authentic / Forged      │
                    │  + Localization Map      │
                    └────────────────────────┘
```

</details>

1. Image is uploaded through the frontend
2. Backend runs it through all three branches in parallel
3. Features are fused and passed to the classifier
4. Result (Authentic / Forged) + a localization map is returned

<br/>

