## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

| Requirement | Version |
|---|---|
| Python | 3.9+ |
| Node.js | 18+ |
| pip / npm | latest |

### 1️⃣ Clone the repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Sw4pn33/Passive-Image-Forgery-Detection-College-Major-Project.git
cd Passive-Image-Forgery-Detection-College-Major-Project
```

### 2️⃣ Set up the dataset & model
```bash
python download_dataset.py
python dataset_setup.py
python download_model.py
```

### 3️⃣ Run the backend
```bash
cd backend
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
```

### 4️⃣ Run the frontend
```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open `http://localhost:3000` and upload an image to test it out 🎉

<br/>

## 🧪 Training from Scratch

Want to retrain the model on your own split of CASIA v1.0?

```bash
python kaggle_train.py
```

This script is Kaggle-notebook-ready — drop it into a Kaggle kernel with the CASIA dataset attached and run end-to-end.

<br/>

## 📊 Dataset

Trained and evaluated on **CASIA v1.0**, a widely-used benchmark for image forgery detection containing authentic and tampered (spliced / copy-moved) images across multiple categories.

Sample test images are included under [`/samples`](./samples) for quick demo purposes.

